$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-[(4-Methyl-2-nitrophenyl)thio]benzoic Acid (3a). A mixture of
4-bromo-3-nitrotoluene (1a, 4.54 g, 21 mmol), thiosalicylic acid (2, 3.1
g, 20 mmol), Cu powder (365 mg, 5.74 mmol), and K2CO3 (6.4 g, 46.4 mmol)
in DMF (50 mL) was heated at 65 °C overnight, cooled to room temperature,
and poured to ice-water. The mixture was filtered through a layer of
Celite. The filtrate was made acidic with 6 N HCl and extracted with
CH2Cl2 (70 mL x 3). The combined organic layers were washed with H2O,
dried, and concentrated. The crude product was crystallized from EtOH/H2O
to provide the title compound as a yellowish solid (4.97 g, 86%), mp 189-
191 °C. 2-[(4-Methyl-2-nitrophenyl)thio]benzoic Acid (3a). yield (4.97 g,
86%) 1H NMR: δ 8.13 (dd, 1H, J = 1.6, 7.7 Hz), 7.93 (s, 1H), 7.51 (dd,
1H, J = 1.6, 7.6 Hz), 7.44 (dt, 1H, J = 1.2, 7.6 Hz), 7.25-7.35 (m, 2H),
