$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative Procedure. Substituted
2-chlorobenzaldehyde or 2-chlorobenzonitrile (1 mmol) was stirred, in the
presence of K2CO3 (2 mmol) and 2-mercaptoacetone (1.2 mmol) suspended in
H2O (1 mL), at 90 °C, for 2 h. At the end of the reaction (TLC), the
required product was either isolated by simple filtration of the mixture
or extracted into EtOAc. The product was dried under vacuum at 50 °C.
2-Acetyl-5-nitrobenzo[b]thiophene (1c), yield 86%, White-brown solid. mp
176-178 °C (from Et2O); 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ = 8.86 (1 H, d, J =
1.5 Hz, Harom), 8.47 (1 H, s, Harom), 8.29-8.21 (2 H, m, Harom), 2.66 (3
H, s, CH3). 13C NMR (75 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ = 192.4 (Cq), 147.1 (Cq), 146.7
(Cq), 145.4 (Cq), 139.0 (Cq), 131.5 (CH), 124.5 (CH), 121.7 (CH), 121.1
(CH), 26.6 (CH3). ESI-MS (MeCN): m/z calcd: 221 [M + H]+; found: 222.
HMRS (CI): m/z [M + H]+ calcd for C10H8NO3S: 222.0219; found: 222.0218.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
