$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure A: To a 10 mL glass tube,
CuBr (2.8 mg, 0.02 mmol), 1,10-phenanthroline (3.6 mg, 0.02 mmol), AgSCF3
(62.7 mg, 0.3 mmol), and arylhalide (0.2 mmol) were dissolved in dry
CH3CN (1 mL) under N2 atmosphere. The tube was sealed and the mixture was
stirred at the corresponding temperature for 6 h. After completion of the
reaction, the solvent was removed under vacuum and the residue was
subjected to flash column chromatography on silica gel with a gradient
eluent of petroleum ether and ethyl acetate to provide the product.
4-methyl-2-(2-((trifluoromethyl)thio)phenyl)pyridine (2a) This reaction
was conducted with procedure A in 0.2 mmol scale. The residue was
purified by column chromatography on silica gel with a gradient eluent of
petroleum ether and ethyl acetate (10:1 - 5:1). methyl
3-(4-methylpyridin-2-yl)-4-((trifluoromethyl)thio)benzoate (2i) This
reaction was conducted with procedure A in 0.2 mmol scale. The residue
was purified by column chromatography on silica gel with a gradient
eluent of petroleum ether and ethyl acetate (10:1 - 5:1). The product 2i
(56 mg, 86% yield) as yellow oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.55 (d, J =
5.2 Hz, 1H), 8.25 (d, J = 2.0 Hz, 1H), 8.07 (dd, J = 8.4, 1.6 Hz, 1H),
7.88 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.43 (s, 1H), 7.16 (d, J = 4.8 Hz, 1H), 3.94
(s, 3H), 2.45 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 166.0, 156.3, 148.3,
148.0, 143.2, 132.8 (q, J = 1.5 Hz), 131.5 (q, J = 0.9 Hz), 131.0, 130.5,
129.6, 129.4 (q, J = 310 Hz), 124.3, 123.8, 52.4, 21.1. 19F NMR (376 MHz,
CDCl3) δ -41.05 (s). HRMS: m/z (ESI) calculated [M+H]+: 328.0614,
measured: 328.0625.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative preparation shown, sealed tube used
