$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of OCMe2CMe2OP(S)SC6H4NO2
p-bromonitrobenzene (0.96 gm) was dissolved in 30 ml benzene. To this, a
solution of ammonium tetramethylene dithiophosphate (1.09 gm) was added
slowly and refluxed for ~10 h. The precipitated ammonium bromide was
filtered off. The solvent was removed from the filtrate under reduced
pressure to obtain the desired product, yellow sticky solid. The above
procedure was adopted for all the other reactions. Relevant data are
given in Table II. OCH2CH2CHMeOP(S)SC6H4NO2, yield 1.32 g, 86%. 1H (δ
ppm) 1.5, S, 3H (CH3); 4.4, m, 2H (POCH2); 5.0, m, 1H (POCH) 7.7, m, 4H
(C6H4), 31p (δ ppm) 91.00
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Organic derivatives of alkylene dithiophosphates part III: Synthesis and
properties of 2-(p-nitrophenyl) and 2-(p-nitrobenzoyl) derivatives of
alkylene dithiophosphates
