$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1.2 General procedure for the coupling
reaction 3 mL [Bmim]BF4 was added into a 25 mL two-neck flask equipped
with a condenser tube. The system was vacuumized at 60 °C for 20 min and
charged with nitrogen gas. Halogenated aromatic hydrocarbon 1 mmol, thiol
or thiophenol 1.1 mmol, K2CO3 2 mmol, CuBr 0.05 mmol and L-proline 0.1
mmol were added. The reaction mixture was heated to proper temperature
and stirred for 5 or 10 h. The temperature was lowered to room
temperature to terminate the reaction. The product was extracted with
ethyl ether (5 mL × 3) from the ionic liquid, concentrated and purified
by preparative TLC (prepared by silica gel GF254 made by Qingdao Marine
Chemical Factory, activated before use) or column chromatography [silica
gel, made by Qingdao Marine Chemical Factory, 200-300 mesh; eluant: V
(cyclohexane) : V (ethyl acetate) = 10 : 1]. The ionic liquid containing
CuBr was recovered and recycled. 42917-47-5, 85 %, oil
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
