$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1.2 Synthesis of 2-arylsulfanyl aniline 10 mol
% cuprous iodide, 20 mol % L-proline, 1 mmol K2CO3, 0.5 mmol
N-trifluoroacetyl-o-iodoaryl amine, 0.6 mol aryl thiol and 3 mL ethylene
glycol dimethyl ether were added to a reaction tube. Vacuumizing and
adding high purity nitrogen were repeated three times under the cooling
condition, then the reaction tube was sealed, and stirred for 40 h in 60
°C oil bath. The mixture was cooled to room temperature, 10 mL saturated
salt water and 10 mL ethyl acetate were added. The organic phase was
separated, the aqueous phase was extracted for 3-4 times, combined with
the organic phase, and dried with anhydrous sodium sulfate, then
concentrated via rotary evaporation, the remainder was purified by column
chromatography to give the pure product. 3p, 85 %, pale yellow solid m.p.
62-64°C; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ: 8.22 (s, 1H), 8.05 (s, 1H), 7.33 (s,
1H), 7.14-7.17 (m, 1H), 6.59-6.69 (m, 3H), 3.72 (s, 3H), 2.30 (s, 3H),
2.21 (s, 3H), 2.03 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ: 168.3, 160.2,
140.4, 137.9, 137.3, 133.1, 130.2, 122.1, 118.9, 116.0, 112.3, 111.5,
55.3, 24.9, 20.2, 19.2; IR (KBr) ν: 3335, 2965, 2921, 1690, 1592, 1572,
1510, 1471, 1444, 1389, 1284, 1230, 1045 cm-1; MS (ESI) m/z: 302 ([M +
H]+); HRMS (EI) calcd for C17H19NO2S 301.1141, found 301.1137.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of N-[2-(phenylthio)phenyl]-2,2,2-trifluoroacetamide
derivatives via ortho substituent-promoted, copper iodide and
L-proline-catalyzed substitution reaction of
N-(2-iodophenyl)-2,2,2-trifluoroacetamide with benzenethiol
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
