$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of
2-Amino-5-ethoxy/5-fluoro-2'-nitrodiphenylsulfides (IIIa-d)
2-Amino-5-ethoxy/5-fluorobenzenethiol [I, 0.01 mmol] was dissolved in
ethanol (20 ml) containing anhydrous sodium acetate (0.01 mmol) and
halonitrobenzene26(II; 0.01 mmol) in ethanol (10 ml) was added. The
reaction mixture was refluxed for 4 h, concentrated, and cooled in an ice
bath overnight. The solid separated out was filtered and washed with 30%
ethanol. Crystallization from methanol afforded the desired product.
Physical data are recorded in Table I. IIIb, yield 85%. m.p.°C: 86;
Molecular formula: C14H13N2O3SCl; % found (Cald.): C, 51.82 (51.77); H,
4.02 (4.03); N, 8.57 (8.63).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
