$DATUM Synthesis of compound 24 from 18 or 19: To a solution of 19 (0.08 mg,
0.14 mmol) was added 4-Methoxy thiophenol (0.10 mL, 0.81 mmol) in dry DMF
(2 mL) was heated at 140°C for 24 h under nitrogen. The solution was
cooled to room temperature, extracted with CH2Cl2 and water, concentrated
under reduced pressure. The crude mass was purified by column
chromatography using CH2Cl2/hexane (1:5) as the eluent to provide the
solid of 24. Yield of 85 % (yield is 80 % from 18) yellow solid,. m.p. >
300 °C 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 3.78 (s, 3H), 5.74 (s, 2H), 6.19 (s,
2H), 6.75-6.77 (m, 2H), 6.91-7.01 (m, 10H), 7.11 (d, 4H, J = 7.1 Hz),
7.39 (d, 4H, J = 7.1 Hz); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 49.5, 52.0, 55.5,
115.3, 124.0, 124.1, 125.7 (2C), 127.5, 128.7, 130.2, 136.4, 143.6,
143.9, 144.2, 149.3, 158.6; IR(KBr): 3069, 1524, 1492 cm-1; FAB-HRMS
calcd for C41H27NO3S (M+) 613.1712, found 613.1709.
