$DATUM A mixture, of 4-(2,6-difluorophenyl)-pyridine (0.45 g, 2.35 mmol), methyl
mercaptan sodium salt (0.21 g, 3.00 mmol) in DMF 00 mL) was heated at
100°C overnight. The mixture was diluted with EtOAC and saturated NaCl,
the organic layer was dried, filtered, concentrated, and purified by
chromatography to afford 4-(2-thiomethyl-6-fluorophenyl)-pyridine as a
yellow solid (0.44 g, 85%). 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 8.71 (d, 2 H), 7.32 (m, 3
H), 7.07 (d, 1 H), 6.97 t, 1 H), 2.39 (s, 3 H). MS m/z 220 (M+).
