$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 7,8-bis(methylthio)-[5]-helicene (compound 14) Into a dry 10 ml flask
equipped with a stirrer and a condenser under a nitrogen atmosphere were
added 7,8-dibromo-[5]-helicene (500 mg, 1.15 mmol, 1.00 eq) and NaSMe
(485 mg, 6.90 mmol, 6.00 eq) followed by the injection of DMSO and n-BuOH
(both of them 2.0 ml, distilled and dried over 4A molecular sieve). The
catalyst Pd(PPh3)4 (106 mg, 0.090 mmol, 0.080 eq) was added and the
suspension was warmed up to 100°C for 15 hours in an oil bath. The
dissolution was complete at 100°C, the color changed from a deep
yellow-brown suspension to a transparent red solution. After cooling down
to 20°C, dilution with CH2Cl2 (60 ml) and addition of H2O (100 ml), the
organic phase was separated. The aqueous phase was extracted with CH2Cl2
(2x30 ml). The combined organic phases were washed with H2O (2 x 100 ml),
dried over Na2SO4, filtered and the solvent was removed under vacuum. The
crude product (a deep brown oil) was filtrated on a short column of
silica gel with toluene/cyclohexane (10/90) as eluent and a sufficiently
pure product (yellow oil; 360 mg; 85%). It was recrystallized from
toluene/ethanol (1/3) to give analytically pure 15 (245 mg; 68%). M.p.:
248°C (dec.) (yellow crystals); Rf = 0.33 (SiO2; CH2Cl2/petroleum ether;
20/80). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 200.13 MHz, 20°C, TMS, δ ppm): 2.54 (s, 6H, CH3);
7.22 (ddd, 2H, J= 6.8, 6.8, 1.3 Hz); 7.52 (ddd, 2H, J=6.9, 6.9, 1.0 Hz);
7.96 (dd, 2H, J= 8.3, 1.0 Hz); 8.01 (d, 2H, J= 9.1 Hz); 8.26 (d, 2H, J=
8.5 Hz); 8.89 (d, 2H, J= 9.0 Hz). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 50.338 MHz, 20°C, TMS,
δ ppm): 21.15 (SCH3), 124.73; 124.77; 126.79; 127.55; 128.03; 129.62;
130.73; 132.37; 132.89, 140.24 (missing 1C). MS (EI, 70 eV): 370 (M+,
64.4%); 276 (M+ - 2SMe, 11.5%); 169 (51.4%); 160 (27.1%); 153 (35.9%);
138 (M2 +, 100%). HRMS (EI, 70 eV): m/z for C24H18S2 [M+] = calcd:
370.0850; found: 370.0871. Elem. Anal. (%) calcd for C24H18S2: C
(77.80%); H (4.90%); found: C (77.57%); H (5.03).
