$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1.2 Synthesis of polychlorinated diphenyl sulfide 3a-3w 1.2.1 Synthesis
of compounds 3a-3w Chloro-substituted thiophenol (1 mmol) dissolved in 10
mL toluene was placed in round bottom flask, then chloro-substituted
iodobenzene (1 mmol), cesium carbonate (2.5 mmol) and
tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium (0.1 mmol) were added to the
reaction flask. The reaction solution was heated up to 112 °C and
refluxed for 16 h under nitrogen protection, then cooled to room
temperature. The reaction solution was diluted with 100 mL water, the
water phase was extracted with 20 mL petroleum ether 3 time. The
petroleum ether were combined, dried with anhydrous magnesium sulfate,
filtered and concentrated to give the crude product. The crude product
was purified on silica gel column (300-400 mesh) eluted with petroleum
ether to give the desired product. The product was characterized by
LC-MS, IR and NMR spectra and the melting point of the product was
determined. 3a, 83%, white crystal m.p. 48-50 ℃; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz)
δ: 6.84 (d, J = 2.0 Hz, 1H), 7.08 (dd, J = 2.4, 8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.30 (d, J =
8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.40 (s, 4H); IR (KBr) ν: 3437, 1567, 1475, 1448, 1214,
1033, 1014, 820, 501 cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, optimization study, optimized on solvent, amount of
catalyst, base, temperature and time
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Palladium-catalyzed carbon-sulfur bond formation to synthesize
polychlorinated diphenyl sulfides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zhang, Xuesheng; Shi, Jiaqi; Sun, Li; Wang, Zunyao
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Youji Huaxue (2011), 31(7), 1107-1113

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME405 STEP1
$RXN



