$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: In the first stage such a nitro group is
substituted by the action of thioglycolic acid ester in the presence of
K2CO3 in N-methylpyrrolidone or DMF giving S-arylthioglycolic acid ester
II. Methyl 2-(4-nitrophenylsulfanyl)acetate (IId). Yield: 85%. mp 51-52°C
(from MeOH) (50.9-52.4°C). 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 3.66 s (3H), 4.15 s
(2H), 7.52 d (2H, 3J 5.8 Hz), 8.15 d (2H, 3J 5.8 Hz).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative reaction conditions shown,DMF as solvent can be used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM New procedure for nucleophilic sulfonation of aromatic nitro compounds.
Destructive oxidation of S-arylthioglycolic acids esters
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
